/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T22:25:15Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T22:25:15Z","body":"the idiom is get track or find track and then add track or remove track. The integer is like a hidden handle that is hidden from the user.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749535187/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749536286","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104576#issuecomment-2749536286","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104576","id":2749536286,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j4pge","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T22:26:02Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T22:26:02Z","body":"Can you write the proposal form? It is confusing why you want this.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749536286/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924992859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104576#issuecomment-2924992859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104576","id":2924992859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uV9lb","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-31T11:21:56Z","updated_at":"2025-05-31T11:24:58Z","body":"I urge that this API should not be made public easily, as it is very unsafe. This method causes animations to have duplicate tracks with the same path (empty path) of the same track type, but the current animation playback API has no safety measures for this case. It should be noted that animation tracks generate hashes from paths and track cache types and internally store them as unique paths.\r\n\r\n> It works similar to array resize. It may not be the best solution to the problem above but it makes up for it with the benefit, of the array resize algorithm itself, of calling the method only once and setting the tracks afterwards.\r\n\r\nThis comment in the [proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12063) description is correct. The correct approach would be to implement APIs that allow safer manipulation of arrays than `resize()`, such as `sort()`, `concat()` or other methods.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924992859/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]